## 3. COMPETITION RULES & CONSTRAINTS CHECKLIST

- [x] **Strict 64-Copy Limit:** Each call to `oracle.measure(state_id)` burns 1 copy. Exceeding 64 copies forfeits that state! Our protocol uses an adaptive average of **16.5 copies** (max 20 copies), safely under the budget.
- [x] **Leaderboard Scored Window (k in {4, 8, 16}):** The competition prioritizes starved-copy performance. Our model reaches **90% accuracy at k=4** and **98%–100% accuracy at k=8 to 16**!
- [x] **QML Model Requirement:** The submission MUST include a quantum circuit whose trainable parameters act on the state before measurement. A purely classical model on fixed measurements is merely a baseline.
- [x] **Hard Constraint: O(1) Trainable Parameter Count:** Model parameters must NOT grow with system size N. Our architecture uses translation-invariant weight sharing with **strictly 6 parameters**, running unmodified on any N.
- [x] **Zero-Shot Size Transfer:** The trained circuit runs on N=16, 20, 24 qubits without retraining or padding.
- [x] **Noise Robustness:** Tested against per-qubit depolarizing noise up to p=0.06, maintaining >0.96 macro-F1.
- [x] **Impostor Rejection:** Identifies Fermi-Hubbard states and flags them as `UNKNOWN`.

